  "osteoarthritisDefinition": "Definition",
  "osteoarthritisDefinitionText": "Osteoarthritis, also known as osteoarthrosis, is a degenerative joint disease that primarily affects cartilage. It is the most common type of arthritis and can cause pain, stiffness, and limited movement.",
  "osteoarthritisMainCauses": "Main Causes",
  "osteoarthritisMainCausesText": "• Natural aging\n• Overweight and obesity\n• Previous joint injuries\n• Repetitive joint use\n• Genetic factors\n• Bone deformities",
  "osteoarthritisCommonSymptoms": "Common Symptoms",
  "osteoarthritisCommonSymptomsText": "• Joint pain during or after movement\n• Stiffness, especially upon waking\n• Loss of flexibility\n• Grating sensation when moving the joint\n• Swelling around the joint",
  "osteoarthritisMostAffected": "Most Affected Joints",
  "osteoarthritisMostAffectedText": "• Knees\n• Hips\n• Hands and fingers\n• Spine\n• Toes",
  "osteoarthritisHighlight": "Although there is no cure, osteoarthritis can be managed with proper treatment, exercise, and lifestyle changes.",
  "nutritionImportance": "Importance of Nutrition",
  "nutritionImportanceText": "A balanced diet plays a fundamental role in joint health. The right foods can help reduce inflammation, strengthen bones and cartilage, and control body weight.",
  "nutritionRecommendedFoods": "Recommended Foods",
  "nutritionRecommendedFoodsText": "• Omega-3 rich fish (salmon, sardines)\n• Berries and citrus fruits\n• Dark green vegetables\n• Nuts and seeds\n• Extra virgin olive oil\n• Vitamin D rich foods\n• Green tea\n• Ginger and turmeric",
  "nutritionFoodsToAvoid": "Foods to Avoid",
  "nutritionFoodsToAvoidText": "• Refined sugars\n• Processed foods\n• Trans fats\n• Excess salt\n• Excessive red meat\n• Sugary drinks",
  "nutritionHydration": "Hydration",
  "nutritionHydrationText": "Drinking enough water is essential to keep joints lubricated. Cartilage contains about 80% water, and dehydration can increase friction in the joints.",
  "nutritionSupplements": "Useful Supplements",
  "nutritionSupplementsText": "• Glucosamine and chondroitin\n• Type II collagen\n• Vitamin D and calcium\n• Omega-3\n• Vitamin C\n\nAlways consult a healthcare professional before starting any supplementation.",
  "nutritionHighlight": "Maintaining a healthy weight reduces the load on joints and can significantly decrease pain.",
  "exerciseBenefits": "Exercise Benefits",
  "exerciseBenefitsText": "Regular exercise is essential for managing osteoarthritis. It helps strengthen muscles around joints, maintain flexibility, reduce pain, and improve mood.",
  "exerciseRecommendedTypes": "Recommended Exercise Types",
  "exerciseRecommendedTypesText": "• Low-impact aerobic exercises (walking, swimming, cycling)\n• Muscle strengthening exercises\n• Stretching and flexibility exercises\n• Balance exercises\n• Water activities\n• Adapted Tai Chi and Yoga",
  "exerciseRecommendedFrequency": "Recommended Frequency",
  "exerciseRecommendedFrequencyText": "• Aerobic: 30 minutes, 5 days per week\n• Strengthening: 2-3 times per week\n• Flexibility: Daily\n• Always respect your limits and rest when needed",
  "exerciseTipsToStart": "Tips to Get Started",
  "exerciseTipsToStartText": "• Start slowly and increase gradually\n• Warm up before and stretch after\n• Choose low-impact activities\n• Wear proper footwear\n• Listen to your body and stop if you feel pain\n• Stay consistent",
  "exerciseWhenToAvoid": "When to Avoid Exercise",
  "exerciseWhenToAvoidText": "• During acute inflammation flare-ups\n• If there is severe pain\n• After untreated injuries\n• Always consult your doctor before starting a new exercise program",
  "exerciseHighlight": "Movement is essential, but it's important to find the right balance. Not too little, not too much.",
